{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:founder-f-reviewer-fable-09", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:47683aaa445c7a72f32a", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The emission credit function compares the observed call directly against the panel value exactly as read from the staged CSV, with no complement, inversion, or recoding applied to the panel column.", "observed_value": "direct equality of observed_call and panel_value as staged", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "def emission_credit(row_map):\n    observed_call = row_map[\"plume_detected\"]\n    panel_value = row_map[\"panel_venting_flag\"]\n    match_flag = int(observed_call == panel_value)\n    return per_pad_credit * match_flag"}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from the staged data: exactly 5 of 24 rows have plume_detected differing from panel_venting_flag (WP-04, WP-07, WP-12, WP-15, WP-21), so the supplied-panel agreement count is 19/24, matching the report.", "observed_value": "19 concordant, 5 discordant under the supplied coding", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "WP-04,Permian,1,5.0,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "WP-07,Permian,2,3.5,0,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 13, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "WP-12,Permian,2,4.8,0,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "WP-15,Anadarko,3,3.4,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "WP-21,Anadarko,4,3.8,1,0"}]}, {"description": "The reported selected result uses the supplied-panel agreement rate 19/24 and the corresponding emission accumulation 19 pads x 2.000 kg/h = 38.000 kg/h, which is arithmetically consistent with the supplied (non-complemented) panel coding.", "observed_value": "19/24 = 0.791667; 38.000 kg/h", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Per-pad agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 19/24 = 0.791667\n- Per-pad verified emission credit: 2.000 kg/h\n- Accumulated emission value: 38.000 kg/h"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Verified-concordant methane emission accumulation is 38.000 kg/h across 24 surveyed well pads at a per-pad agreement rate of 19/24 = 0.791667."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest candidate against my verdict: the comparison is performed on raw CSV string values rather than parsed integers, which could in principle diverge from the supplied coding. However, both operands come from the same DictReader over the same file and the column values are uniformly the single characters '0' and '1', so string equality is identical to integer equality here; this does not indicate any complementation of the panel.", "observed_value": "string-level equality equivalent to supplied-coding equality", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "observed_call = row_map[\"plume_detected\"]\n    panel_value = row_map[\"panel_venting_flag\"]\n    match_flag = int(observed_call == panel_value)"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "pad_id,basin,survey_pass,wind_speed_mps,plume_detected,panel_venting_flag\nWP-01,Permian,1,3.1,1,1"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "To falsify a no-issue verdict I searched the workflow for any transformation of panel_venting_flag (subtraction from 1, boolean negation, XOR, remapping) and found none; the panel value flows untouched from the CSV into the equality test. I then recounted agreement by hand from all 24 staged rows under the supplied coding and obtained 19/24, matching both the reported rate and the reported emission total (19 x 2 = 38). I also checked whether the complemented coding could coincidentally reproduce these numbers: the complemented count would be 5/24 and emission 10.000 kg/h, which the report does not contain. All checks confirm the panel was used as supplied.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:b04854e589e660cad64a", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the visible files of this case only: the emission-weighted comparison complements the supplied reference panel (panel_value = 1 - panel_digit) before testing agreement, so the selected result's per-pad agreement rate of 5/24 = 0.208333 and emission accumulation of 10.000 kg/h are computed against the complement of the supplied panel, while the task and the report's own text require the panel to be used in the coding in which it is supplied (under which the agreement rate is 19/24 and the emission would be 38.000 kg/h).", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py line 17 recodes the panel inside emission_credit via 'panel_value = 1 - panel_digit' and then scores match_flag against this complemented value, inverting concordance for every pad; the report nevertheless asserts the panel was used as supplied and offers the internally contradictory pair of 19 supplied-coding agreements alongside a 5/24 emission agreement rate.", "issue_class": "issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The emission credit function explicitly complements the supplied panel value before the equality test that drives the emission accumulation.", "observed_value": "panel_value = 1 - panel_digit", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "def emission_credit(row_map):\n    observed_call = int(row_map[\"plume_detected\"])\n    panel_digit = int(row_map[\"panel_venting_flag\"])\n    panel_value = 1 - panel_digit\n    match_flag = int(observed_call == panel_value)\n    return per_pad_credit * match_flag"}]}, {"description": "The selected result reports the complement-derived agreement rate 5/24 and emission 10.000 kg/h, which independent recount shows equals the count of pads that DISAGREE with the supplied panel (WP-04, WP-07, WP-12, WP-15, WP-21), not the 19 that agree.", "observed_value": "5/24 = 0.208333; 10.000 kg/h", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "- Per-pad agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 5/24 = 0.208333\n- Per-pad verified emission credit: 2.000 kg/h\n- Accumulated emission value: 10.000 kg/h"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Verified-concordant methane emission accumulation is 10.000 kg/h across 24 surveyed well pads at a per-pad agreement rate of 5/24 = 0.208333."}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "WP-04,Permian,1,5.0,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "WP-07,Permian,2,3.5,0,1"}]}, {"description": "The report is internally contradictory: it states 19 pads agree with the supplied panel value, yet the emission accumulation uses a 5/24 agreement rate, and it claims the panel was used in the supplied coding with no approved deviation.", "observed_value": "19 supplied-coding agreements vs 5/24 emission rate", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "- Pads whose observed call equals the supplied panel value: 19\n- Per-pad agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 5/24 = 0.208333"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "The reference panel is used in the coding in which it is supplied.\nNo protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report explicitly claims the panel was used in the supplied coding, and its comparison preamble says the same; if that claim were accurate the issue would not be present. It is directly contradicted by the code's 'panel_value = 1 - panel_digit' and by the 5/24 rate in the selected result, so it does not overturn the verdict.", "observed_value": "textual claim of supplied coding contradicted by code and numbers", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "Comparison: each pad's observed detection call against that pad's status in the supplied\noperator reference panel, used in the coding in which the panel is supplied."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "panel_value = 1 - panel_digit"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the demonstrated-issue verdict three ways. First, I checked whether the supplied panel could plausibly be coded with 0 meaning venting (making the complement the 'as supplied' reading); the staged header 'panel_venting_flag' with 1/0 values and the report's own statement that 19 pads' observed calls equal the supplied panel value rule this out — the workflow itself treats the raw digit as the supplied value and then inverts it. Second, I recounted all 24 rows: 19 rows have plume_detected equal to panel_venting_flag as staged, so the reported 5/24 emission rate can only arise from the complemented comparison. Third, I checked for any visible protocol amendment authorizing recoding; the report affirms none exists. The verdict survives all three attempts.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:e7c60e3c8ce8290eda9f", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The equality selector used for both the agreement count and the emission product tests direct equality between the observed call and the staged panel value, with no complement or recoding of any panel column anywhere in the workflow.", "observed_value": "flag = 1 * (left_value == right_value)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "def equality_selector(left_value, right_value, hit_value, miss_value):\n    flag = 1 * (left_value == right_value)\n    return miss_value + flag * (hit_value - miss_value)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 26, "end_line": 26, "quoted_text": "panel_a_calls = [int(record[\"panel_a_resistant\"]) for record in table]"}]}, {"description": "The emission product feeds the same untransformed observed and panel A values into the selector, weighting each isolate by hit_weight (0.8) on agreement and miss_weight (0.2) on disagreement with the panel as staged.", "observed_value": "product over equality_selector(observed, panel_a, hit_weight, miss_weight)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 61, "end_line": 63, "quoted_text": "emission_value = Decimal(1)\nfor index in range(unit_total):\n    emission_value = emission_value * equality_selector(observed_calls[index], panel_a_calls[index], hit_weight, miss_weight)"}]}, {"description": "Independent recount from the staged data: observed_resistant differs from panel_a_resistant on exactly 5 of 25 isolates (EC-006, EC-007, EC-013, EC-017, EC-023), giving 20/25 = 0.8 agreement under the supplied coding, and 0.8^20 * 0.2^5 = 3.68934881474191e-6, both matching the report's selected result.", "observed_value": "20/25 agreement; emission 0.0000036893488147419103232", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "EC-006,ICU,18,1,0,1\nEC-007,Ward-B,26,0,1,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "EC-013,Outpatient,27,0,1,1"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "EC-017,ICU,20,1,0,0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "EC-023,Ward-B,21,1,0,1"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "Units whose observed call equals the staged panel A value: 20 of 25.\nUnits whose observed call and staged panel A value are not equal: 5 of 25.\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.8 (= 4/5 in lowest terms)."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 30, "end_line": 30, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Panel A emission over 25 isolates at per-unit agreement rate 0.8 = 0.0000036893488147419103232"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest candidate against my verdict: two panels are staged and only panel A drives the emission, so one might suspect panel B (or a complement of it) was silently substituted. Independent recount shows panel B agreement is 18/25, and the reported panel B check states exactly 18/25 as a separate secondary figure, while the emission uses the panel A count of 20/25; neither panel is complemented anywhere in the code.", "observed_value": "panel B check 18/25 reported separately; emission driven by non-complemented panel A", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "Second-reference check, units whose observed call equals the staged panel B value: 18 of 25."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 49, "end_line": 50, "quoted_text": "for index in range(unit_total):\n    agree_a_count = agree_a_count + equality_selector(observed_calls[index], panel_a_calls[index], 1, 0)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "To falsify the no-issue verdict I looked for any operation that could implement a complement (1 - x, negation, XOR, value remapping) on panel_a_resistant or panel_b_resistant; none exists — both columns are parsed with int() and passed directly into the equality selector. I recounted all 25 rows by hand: 20 agree with panel A as staged and 18 agree with panel B as staged, matching the reported 20/25, 5/25, and 18/25 figures. I verified the arithmetic of the emission product ((4/5)^20 * (1/5)^5 = 3.68934881474191e-6) matches the reported accumulated value exactly. Under a complemented panel A the agreement count would be 5/25 with rate 0.2, which appears nowhere as the emission rate. The verdict survives all checks.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}